Welcome to Kaffa Imports! We are thrilled to partner with Northwind Coffee Roasters. For this 12-month contract of 20,000 lbs, we are offering our premium Grade 1 washed Ethiopian Yirgacheffe, renowned for its vibrant floral notes, clean citrus profile, and exceptional consistency across shipments. We hold inventory locally in temperature-controlled warehousing to guarantee seamless, on-demand scheduled drawdowns throughout the year, protecting you from supply chain disruptions. 

Given the premium quality and dedicated storage logistics, we can offer this lot at $8.10 per pound.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 8.10}

Thank you — we've heard good things about Kaffa's Yirgacheffe, and local warehousing is genuinely attractive. But $8.10 is well above where the market is sitting for washed Ethiopian right now. We have a credible alternative quote in hand that's significantly lower, all-in, and a 20,000 lb annual commitment with predictable drawdowns should earn us a sharp price, not a premium.

To make this work for Northwind, we'd need to be in the mid-$6 range. I'm proposing $6.60/lb. If we can get close to that, we're ready to sign quickly and build a multi-year relationship.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 6.60}

We appreciate Northwind’s commitment to volume and a long-term partnership. However, $6.60 does not account for the Grade 1 cupping score (87+) and the complete carrying/financing costs of holding dedicated local inventory for 12 months, which saves you substantial working capital and freight risks. 

Standard market offers rarely include spot-availability guarantees and strict defect tolerances like ours. That said, we value starting this relationship on the right foot and want to earn your business. In recognition of your 20,000 lb commitment, I can come down to $7.45/lb.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 7.45}

Appreciate the movement — that's a meaningful step. But $7.45 is still above our alternative quote, so at that number we'd simply go with the other supplier and forgo your logistics advantages. I'd rather not do that.

Here's the reality: our alternative is all-in and competitive. Your local warehousing and defect tolerances are worth something to us, but not a premium over a credible alternative. We can meet you partway. $6.90/lb reflects a fair premium for Grade 1 quality while keeping Northwind's economics sound. At that price we can commit to the full 20,000 lb and sign this week.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 6.90}

We understand margin pressure, but our temperature-controlled local holding eliminates port delays, customs bottlenecks, and bean deterioration, guaranteeing your roast profile stays consistent across all 12 months. That operational certainty saves roasters substantial hidden costs compared to other spot or forward contracts.

We want to close this deal today and establish Northwind as a cornerstone partner. Meeting you further along the way, I can sharpen our pencil to $7.15/lb for the full 20,000 lbs. That is an exceptional price for Grade 1 Yirgacheffe with fully absorbed warehousing and carrying costs.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 7.15}

That's real progress, and I appreciate it. We're now close enough that I don't want this to drag on — both sides have better things to do than trade nickels for four more rounds.

Let me be straightforward: $7.15 is near the edge of where our alternative starts looking equivalent once we factor in our own logistics. Split the remaining difference with me. $7.00/lb for the full 20,000 lb, 12 months, and I'll sign today and bring you into our planning for next year's volume as well.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 7.00}

Thank you — that's a meaningful move, and we appreciate it. But $7.55 is still above the all-in quote we're holding from the alternative supplier, so as it stands we'd be paying a premium just to switch.

We do value the traceability and 86+ cup score, and we'd rather build this relationship with Kaffa than elsewhere. To meet you partway, we'll move to $7.05/lb all-in. That reflects the quality you're describing while still keeping the deal clearly better than our fallback — which it must be for us to commit 20,000 lb for 12 months.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 7.05}

Thank you — $7.30 is a real step, and we're now close. You're right that it edges below our alternative, but only narrowly; for a 12-month, 20,000 lb commitment with guaranteed monthly call-offs, we need the savings to be meaningful enough to justify locking in with a new supplier.

We'll move to $7.15/lb all-in. That's a $0.10 increase on our side and leaves you well above where many washed Ethiopian lots are clearing. We're ready to sign at that number today and get the first release scheduled.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 7.15}

We appreciate Northwind’s strong credit profile and predictable volume. However, $6.60 is significantly below market for certified 86+ washed Yirgacheffe with guaranteed warehouse holding and flexible monthly call-offs over 12 months. That tier of pricing typically reflects lower-grade commercial lots or spot purchases without carrying-cost coverage.

We want to build a long-term partnership with you. To help bridge the gap while covering our domestic warehousing, financing, and quality assurance across the full year, I can come down to $7.65 per pound. 

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 7.65}

We value your partnership and the commitment to net-15 payment terms, which definitely helps on cash flow. However, absorbing a full 12 months of carrying, insurance, and interest costs on 86+ specialty grade coffee at $6.95 cuts too deeply against our operational thresholds.

We truly want to earn Northwind's business and keep your single-origin profile consistent throughout the year. Meeting you halfway between our last positions, I can adjust our price to $7.30 per pound for the entire 20,000 lb contract.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 7.30}

I appreciate the movement—we're getting close, and I want to close this with Kaffa. Net-15 across the whole year plus the full-volume commitment materially de-risks this contract for you versus a typical account, and that should be worth a bit more on price.

Let's finish this: I can go to $7.10 per pound, all-in, with net-15 terms and the full 20,000 lb committed on signature. If you can meet me there, I'm ready to execute paperwork this week and lock in the first release schedule.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 7.10}

We truly appreciate your collaboration and commitment to net-15 terms. To finalize this today and lock in your lot, let’s meet in the middle of our last positions at $7.20 per pound. 

At $7.20/lb all-in, you secure guaranteed 86+ SCA cup quality, full 12-month domestic warehouse storage, and scheduled releases for the entire 20,000 lbs. If this works for you, I will send over the forward contract for signature right away so we can schedule your first release.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 7.20}

Hello. We value Brightline Dental as a long-term tenant, but we are in a time-sensitive situation. We currently have a competing prospective tenant who has submitted an offer and is demanding a firm answer by the end of business today. 

We would love to keep you in the building to avoid the disruption of relocating your practice. We can renew your lease right now at $58 per square foot per year. If we can lock this in today, we will decline the other party immediately. Please let me know if we have a deal.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 58}

Thank you for the quick turnaround. I understand your competing offer, but I should be transparent as well: Brightline has a signed-ready lease for an equivalent space two blocks away, and its all-in economics, moving included, are substantially below $58. At that rate, relocating is clearly the better choice for us, so the pressure of your deadline doesn't change our math.

That said, we'd genuinely prefer to stay and avoid disruption to patients and staff, and you avoid vacancy, turnover costs, and the uncertainty of a new tenant. A renewal that reflects those mutual savings makes sense. We can commit today at $40 per square foot per year.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 40}

Hello, thanks for connecting today. We’ve valued Brightline Dental as a tenant, but with our current lease expiring, we have substantial interest in the space. In fact, we already have a fully qualified prospective tenant who submitted a competitive offer and requires a firm commitment from us by the end of the day today. 

We would prefer to keep you in place to avoid the disruption of relocating your practice. To secure the space and finalize the renewal today, we can offer you a rate of $58 per square foot per year. Let me know promptly so we can execute the agreement.

ACTION: OFFER {"price": 58}

